#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/intrinsics/macro/wgmma_macro_generator/index.rst:43
msgid ""
"Shared by the WGMMA and UMMA descriptor builders. A K-major operand wider "
"than one swizzle atom decodes with its K mode split into ``(atom, panels)``, "
"and that panel sub-mode's stride is the step the atom offset formulas need. "
"It cannot be reconstructed as ``mn_extent * swizzle_atom_elems``, which only "
"holds when the operand covers its whole buffer -- for a slice the MN extent "
"shrinks while the panel spacing does not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/intrinsics/macro/wgmma_macro_generator/index.rst:50
msgid ""
"``k_mode`` is the operand tile's K mode in element space (post-"
"``restrict``). Returns ``None`` only when no panel step is needed: an MN-"
"major operand, or a layout with a single K panel, where the ``ki // "
"k_atom_size`` factor the step is multiplied by is always zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/intrinsics/macro/wgmma_macro_generator/index.rst:55
msgid ""
"A swizzled multi-panel layout whose K mode is not the canonical ``(atom, "
"panels):(1, panel_stride)`` asserts rather than falling back to the extent-"
"based reconstruction: that fallback is precisely the defect this decode "
"exists to remove, so re-entering it silently would reintroduce a wrong-code "
"path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/intrinsics/macro/wgmma_macro_generator/index.rst:0
