#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/intrinsics/macro/wgmma_macro_generator/index.rst:66
msgid ""
"Hopper WGMMA accepts ``N`` in ``[8, 256]`` with ``N % 8 == 0``, so an extent "
"such as 96 or 160 is a single legal instruction.  Selecting "
"``gcd(warp_col_tiles, 256)`` instead splits those into n32 / n16 atoms and "
"gives up most of the tensor-core throughput."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/intrinsics/macro/wgmma_macro_generator/index.rst:71
msgid ""
"Widening is restricted to multiples of 16 for two independent reasons: ``N % "
"16 == 8`` already miscomputes for ``warp_cols > 1`` (issue #2593), and the "
"integer instruction tables in ``wgmma.h`` / ``wgmma_sp.h`` only instantiate "
"multiples of 16 (plus 8 and 24), so a wider ``N % 16 == 8`` would not even "
"compile for the s8 path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/intrinsics/macro/wgmma_macro_generator/index.rst:80
msgid ""
"Pre-computed WGMMA descriptor parameters, produced by :func:"
"`compute_gmma_descriptor` (a port of CuTe ``make_gmma_desc``) and consumed "
"by ``init_wgmma_*_desc()`` and ``wgmma_*_atom()``."
msgstr ""

